  "10.60.40.10(1)": {"explanation": "In the RT zone, the maximum height is the HT number on the Height Overlay Map, or 10.0 m where there is none. A houseplex may always reach at least 10.0 m. On a major street, a townhouse may reach 13.0 m and an apartment building 19.0 m, or the HT number if that is higher.", "code_refs": "none"},
  "10.60.40.10(2)": {"explanation": "The maximum number of storeys is the ST number on the Height Overlay Map. Where there is none, this rule sets no storey limit. Houseplexes are exempt. On a major street, a townhouse may have four storeys and an apartment building six, or the ST number if that is higher.", "code_refs": "none"}
